---
description: Prefer TokenSave MCP tools over scanning the repo with grep/glob/read
alwaysApply: true
---

When TokenSave MCP tools are available (`tokensave_search`, `tokensave_context`, `tokensave_node`, `tokensave_status`, and related graph tools), use them for code discovery before raw file reads. This applies to Cloud Agents and local agents.

Start with `tokensave_context` or `tokensave_search`. Use `tokensave_node` or `tokensave_body` for a symbol the graph already named. Open a file with Read only after the graph names that file, or when you need lines the graph did not return. Do not use Grep, Glob, wide Read sweeps, or Explore subagents while TokenSave is connected.

Do not narrate token-savings metrics unless the user asks. If tokensave is not installed or the MCP server is disconnected, fall back to the usual search tools.
